shipped-build-temp-flags.patch -- reconstruction of one behaviour of the compiler build Capcom shipped
RE4 with, which differs from SN's v1.79 source drop (2003-06) at exactly these six sites of
gcc/function.c.  Applied by build.sh after linux-host.patch.

What it changes: stock GCC 2.95 `assign_temp` and the five `assign_parms` parameter-slot sites call
`MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (mem, aggregate)`, whose "not aggregate" branch SETS `MEM_SCALAR_P` on the
frame slot.  With the flag, alias.c `fixed_scalar_and_varying_struct_p` declares a fixed scalar
frame slot disjoint from every `MEM_IN_STRUCT_P` store through a varying pointer, so a reload of a
compiler temporary (or of an address-taken parameter) may be scheduled above such stores.  The
shipped build does not do that: non-aggregate stack temps and parm slots carry NEITHER flag here,
so they are ordered against struct stores like any other MEM.

Visible case: the polymorphic copy `*p = *src` of a class with a vptr (cp/class.c sets
TYPE_NONCOPIED_PARTS = (vtable, vfield), expr.c MODIFY_EXPR runs save_noncopied_parts: vptr saved
to an `assign_temp` slot, 24-byte block move, vptr restored).  The original binary reloads the vptr
after the tail stores of the block move (esp0a Esp0a_Trans / SetFreeWork, esp0e Esp0e_Trans); stock
v1.79 hoists the reload above them.

Evidence (2026-09-11, ~/.cache/ccpatch harness: every prodg_cc unit of build.ninja compiled with the
installed v1.79 cc1plus/cc1 and with the patched pair, masked per-function compare against the split
objects):
  * 763 units, 19119 functions identical before; 0 regressions, 0 changed objects with the sources
    of the tree as they were (every previously affected site carried a source workaround).
  * esp0a with its four copies written `*base = *esp; *e.p = *base; *base = *this; *p = *base;` is
    6/6 identical, esp0e with `*p = *esp` is 8/8 identical (4/6 and 7/8 without the patch).
  * Widening the edit to put_reg_into_stack (function.c 1740) regresses item `combine` (a #17-pinned
    function) for no gain, so the shipped build differs at assign_temp + assign_parms only.
  * An earlier run (AGENTS.md "Structural tag hunt (2026-09-11)") listed 7 more newly identical
    functions (objRobo x3, sce_com SceChapterEnd, t_se_at x3); those did not reproduce against the
    committed sources with the same edit -- they were concurrent source edits by other agents that
    landed between that run's base and variant builds, not compiler effects.

diff -ruN a/gcc/function.c b/gcc/function.c
--- a/gcc/function.c	2026-09-11 06:36:24.585489460 +0200
+++ b/gcc/function.c	2026-09-11 06:36:24.586489474 +0200
@@ -1169,7 +1169,8 @@
 	size = TREE_INT_CST_LOW (TYPE_ARRAY_MAX_SIZE (type));
 
       tmp = assign_stack_temp_for_type (mode, size, keep, type);
-      MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (tmp, AGGREGATE_TYPE_P (type));
+      if (AGGREGATE_TYPE_P (type))
+	MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (tmp, 1);
       return tmp;
     }
 
@@ -4543,7 +4544,8 @@
 	  /* If this is a memory ref that contains aggregate components,
 	     mark it as such for cse and loop optimize.  Likewise if it
 	     is readonly.  */
-	  MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, aggregate);
+	  if (aggregate)
+	    MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, 1);
 	  RTX_UNCHANGING_P (stack_parm) = TREE_READONLY (parm);
 	  MEM_ALIAS_SET (stack_parm) = get_alias_set (parm);
 	}
@@ -4685,7 +4687,8 @@
 
 	  /* If this is a memory ref that contains aggregate components,
 	     mark it as such for cse and loop optimize.  */
-	  MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, aggregate);
+	  if (aggregate)
+	    MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, 1);
 	}
 #endif /* 0 */
 
@@ -4742,7 +4745,8 @@
 
 		  /* If this is a memory ref that contains aggregate
 		     components, mark it as such for cse and loop optimize.  */
-		  MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, aggregate);
+		  if (aggregate)
+		    MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, 1);
 		}
 
 	      else if (PARM_BOUNDARY % BITS_PER_WORD != 0)
@@ -4799,7 +4803,8 @@
 	    {
 	      DECL_RTL (parm)
 		= gen_rtx_MEM (TYPE_MODE (TREE_TYPE (passed_type)), parmreg);
-	      MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (DECL_RTL (parm), aggregate);
+	      if (aggregate)
+		MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (DECL_RTL (parm), 1);
 	    }
 	  else
 	    DECL_RTL (parm) = parmreg;
@@ -5059,7 +5064,8 @@
 					  GET_MODE_SIZE (GET_MODE (entry_parm)), 0);
 		  /* If this is a memory ref that contains aggregate components,
 		     mark it as such for cse and loop optimize.  */
-		  MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, aggregate);
+		  if (aggregate)
+		    MEM_SET_IN_STRUCT_P (stack_parm, 1);
 		}
 
 	      if (promoted_mode != nominal_mode)
